.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH orbit-login 1  "login " 
.SH NAME
orbit\-login \- Sign this device in to a server. The password is read from ORBIT_PASSWORD or stdin
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBorbit login\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-totp\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIURL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sign this device in to a server. The password is read from ORBIT_PASSWORD or stdin
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one JSON object per result, with `"v":1`, instead of text
.TP
\fB\-\-totp\fR \fI<TOTP>\fR
The current two\-factor code, if the account has one
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR [default: orbit\-cli]

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable ANSI colors
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIURL\fR>

.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  orbit login https://orbit.example.com
  orbit login https://orbit.example.com \-\-totp 123456
  echo "$PASSWORD" | orbit login https://orbit.example.com \-\-name laptop
